					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/psul" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2156983); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2156983&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607418200" alt="psul" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2156983)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/psul" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2156983); return false;" >psul</a></span> <span class="odate time_1479892349 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">23 Nov 2016 09:12</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2696461">
									

<p>I'm struggling a bit with suspension of disbelief for this one. Principally:</p>
<ul>
<li>Containment Procedures seem a bit lax. Why hasn't the entire town of Freshwater been locked up as anomalous (by virtue of immunity to the oil), or at least quarantined (to stop the annual tourist attendance)?</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>You never quite make the link between &quot;perceives all smells as 2889 oil&quot;, and &quot;wants to go to Freshwater&quot;. Essentially this is a compulsion effect, and while I can understand the desire to obscure that fact, it means the progression of the story doesn't necessarily follow.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>I don't think that municipalities have the power to enact capital laws. Especially in Vermont, which doesn't have the death penalty generally. If you want to go down that road, shouldn't the Foundation be enquiring into how such a law was passed?</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>I don't understand the need for the paragraph about bodily fluids being replaced with 2889 oil. It doesn't pay off later in the story, or seem particularly relevant to the subtext / backstory of Cyparissus, and I don't think it's necessary for scene-setting. For me, it's part of where the skip crosses the &quot;Conservation of WTF&quot; line.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>In the logs, if the mumbling is unintelligible, how does Klein know that the D-Class is mimicking it?</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>There are a few items of description in the logs that don't really work based on the view being from a body-camera attached to the D-Class. For example &quot;the team follows D-19245&quot; wouldn't be seen on the body camera, and neither would it be clear that the young man had cut the D-Class' throat.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>It seems strange that none of the Foundation team made an attempt to discharge their weapons during the attack.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>Considering that this is based on the Cyparissus story, it is odd to have the idea of the mourning young man and his deer companion suddenly turn out to be bloodthirsty monsters. That seems to do a disservice to the themes of the myth, and be a bit of an obvious/simplistic way to end the story.</li>
</ul>

							</div>

								
					
